  "course_description": "Every semester. Introductory workshop in poetry writing. Counts as a prerequisite for 300-level intermediate workshops but not for Advanced Fiction, Advanced Poetry, or Advanced Playwriting. May not be repeated for credit.",
  "course_notes": "(Permission Required Prior to Enrollment) Application required. If accepted, YOU MUST ATTEND THE FIRST CLASS session to remain enrolled. Class description and application form are available on the Creative Writing Program website: https://creativewriting.emory.edu/academics/applications.html Please email nora.lewis@emory.edu if you have any questions. In this class, we will engage in a dynamic exploration of the craft of poetry writing. We'll pursue poetry as a vital and potentially radical art form with much to contribute to contemporary cultural dialogue. To that end, we will undertake a variety of in- and out-of-class writing experiments and read adventurously among contemporary poets. Across the arc of the semester, you will construct a portfolio of your own poetry--one that showcases the scope and depth of your work and demonstrates incisive examples of self-reflection and revision. Additionally, you can look forward to making a collaborative video poem and contributing to our class zine.",
